9/7 scourge infused empire
copies the scourge deep/baseinfo, but into new files and with a new name.
Note that one of the upsides of redoign all the base/deep info is that I can drop the old scourge Fireteam code and use the new stuff.

Player start with a Scourge Builder Flagship. Several other Builders are seeded around the galaxy for you to claim.
Builders are upgraded with Science, and can't upgrade any structure to a higher mark level than their mark level.

You have a very slow base Essence income (upgradable with Science).

Builders plant Flowers, which use the Sappers mechanic; you plant them, you defend them, they flower, you harvest. Essence is what you farm. Done by hacking, planting costs Essence. You can build Expensive flowers (must be on AI controlled planets) or cheap flowers (can be anywhere). Expensive flowers give way more Essence, they're what you want to use. Harvesting a flower triggers an exo (sized based on the amount of essence).

You use Essence to build Armories/Spawner/Fortress, and upgrade their mark levels. Do all this stuff with Hacking (hacks must be able to cost essence).

Note the Builders are owned by the Player, but the other scourge units are their own faction; we use the DirectBuild.cs code to do this.
Needs an Intensity field, and an CPA Counterblow field, the enemy response is big CPAs (units dropped immediately as part of the CPA faction). Strength based on  numSpawners * AIP.

Needs a Notification for "Structures ready to upgrade", since they still use the XP mechanic.

We define some Outguard you can summon; Swarm Calls, in two forms. One is "Summon all the Scourge warriors", the other is "summon only units in offensive fireteams". These will call all the appropriate scourge units to that planet. It costs essence (or hell is just free on a timer) and lasts for a few minutes.
Also a "All units defend" outguard that causes all scourge units to drop their non-defensive fireteams, then to build 100% defensive fireteams.
When any outguard vanishes, the swarm becomes "confused" for a bit. They all drop their firetams and remake them. Note that we may need to make them run back to random spawners/armories if we have trouble with the "remake fireteams" safely.


I need to have code that says "No hybrids of a given type untill you have a tech".

There's a structure on the map to unlock Spire Scourge, but it will cost 15 AIP.


